  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reinforced capacity of ILO offices and regional constituents to develop, implement, monitor and evaluate result-based Decent Work Programmes and other development frameworks at the regional and sub-regional levels</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Country programming is a central element of the ILO&#x2019;s results-based management approach, aligning national priorities with global strategies. The ILO Governing Body and International Labour Conference advocate for Decent Work Country Programmes (DWCPs) in collaboration with national constituents. Where DWCPs aren&apos;t feasible, biennial programmes are developed. The ongoing UN reform enhances the UN development system&apos;s efficiency, emphasizing the UN Sustainable Development Cooperation Frameworks (UNSDCF) as the main planning tool. DWCPs should derive from the UNSDCF. Effective DWCPs have clear priorities and active governance by constituents. The main goal is to build capacity within the ILO and its constituents for effective programme implementation and evaluation.</narrative>
  </description>
